  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1025 PM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nNo significant changes were made to the long term forecast at this\ntime, with the main theme still being hot and mostly dry conditions\nthrough the week. An elongated upper high is expected to center \nitself over the desert SW, while occasional disturbances pass \nnorth of the ridge onto the central Plains. There ridge is \nsuppressed enough that some of these disturbances could bring \nprecip into the northern portions of the forecast area, but this \nis not well- captured by the coarser model guidance at this stage,\nwhich keep precip confined to the higher terrain of NM. Temps are\nlikely to be hot, with highs near 100 on the Caprock and into the\nlow/mid 100s off the Caprock, which may necessitate more Heat \nAdvisories off the Caprock at times next week. May also need to \nkeep an eye on locally enhanced fire danger on Monday, as SW winds\nare forecast to be on the breezy side (sustained winds 15-20 mph,\ngusts 25-30 mph) and minimum RH values fall below 20 percent in \nthe afternoon.",
